# Node.js Learnings
## Steps for creating Node.js app
1. make sure you have Node.js installed and added to PATH
2. make sure you have npm (node modules) installed, usually included with Node.js
3. create package.json by either
    1. manually creating the file and textContent
    2. generating it with npm in terminal Console in your working directory, with:
        - ```npm init```

## Steps for working with Nodemon
1. Install Nodemon with either:
    - ```npm install --save-dev nodemon``` or 
    - ```npm install -D nodemon```
3. Edit package.json "scripts", add: 
    - ```"dev": "nodeman server.js"``` (or whatever file start is)
4. Start server/Nodeman with:
    - ```npm run dev```

## Usefull packages
### 1. sanitize-html
install with: ```npm install sanitize-html```

import with: ```import sanitizeHtml from 'sanitize-html'```
    
doku: [npm package sanitize-html](https://www.npmjs.com/package/sanitize-html)

## Ignoring installed packages when commiting
add to .gitignore with:
- ``node_modules/``

other possibly useful files and folders to ignore:
- githubs gitignore repo [Node.gitignore](https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Node.gitignore)

